WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:15.336
I still couldn't think of an invention to help Molly.

2
00:00:15.337 --> 00:00:19.435
I did suddenly get an idea for the ending of our story though.

3
00:00:19.436 --> 00:00:25.623
It happened when I was pouring myself some Crunchy Oats cereal on Wednesday morning.

4
00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:30.797
I shook the last few crumbs into my bowl.

5
00:00:30.798 --> 00:00:35.353
I tried to get a new box from the cupboard, but I couldn't reach it.

6
00:00:35.354 --> 00:00:40.125
Even when I stood on a stool, the box was just out of reach.

7
00:00:40.126 --> 00:00:44.224
"Mom, I can't reach the cereal!" I called.

8
00:00:44.225 --> 00:00:47.881
My mom was in the living room, putting on her coat.

9
00:00:47.882 --> 00:00:51.191
"I'm late for work, Iggy," she said.

10
00:00:51.192 --> 00:00:54.131
"Please ask your brother to help."

11
00:00:54.132 --> 00:00:59.390
"He won't do it!" I said. "He never helps me."

12
00:00:59.391 --> 00:01:05.697
I don't think my mom heard me, because she said good-bye and hurried out the door.

13
00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:11.596
"You took the last chocolate granola bar," said Tate, staring at me.

14
00:01:11.597 --> 00:01:14.582
"And now you're eating all the Crunchy Oats!"

15
00:01:14.583 --> 00:01:17.696
"There's a brand-new box," I started to say.

16
00:01:17.697 --> 00:01:19.352
"But I can't . . ."

17
00:01:19.353 --> 00:01:23.097
To my surprise, Tate smiled at me.

18
00:01:23.098 --> 00:01:25.662
"I'm just kidding," he said.

19
00:01:25.663 --> 00:01:28.431
"I'll get the cereal for you."

20
00:01:28.432 --> 00:01:33.428
Tate reached up and grabbed the box of Crunchy Oats cereal.

21
00:01:33.429 --> 00:01:36.240
"Gee, thanks!" I said.

22
00:01:36.241 --> 00:01:39.801
"All you have to do is ask," said Tate.

23
00:01:39.802 --> 00:01:42.536
"What?" I blinked in surprise.

24
00:01:42.537 --> 00:01:45.457
All you have to do is ask?

25
00:01:45.458 --> 00:01:48.308
That was it!

26
00:01:48.309 --> 00:01:54.477
The boy in our story could ask the giant vacuum to give his brother back.

27
00:01:54.478 --> 00:01:57.615
The giant vacuum was friendly and gentle.

28
00:01:57.616 --> 00:02:03.531
The vacuum would be happy to return Jack's stuff, along with his big brother.

29
00:02:03.532 --> 00:02:07.727
And Jack would be happy to have his big brother around again.

30
00:02:07.728 --> 00:02:09.168
Just like me.

31
00:02:09.169 --> 00:02:12.893
Once in a while anyway.

32
00:02:12.894 --> 00:02:16.602
Molly loved my plan for our story ending.

33
00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:20.874
We titled our last chapter "Just Ask."

34
00:02:20.875 --> 00:02:27.880
As we wrote the final words, I got the best idea ever—the one I'd been hoping to get.

35
00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:33.258
"Why don't you tell Lucy you can't sleep because of the monster show?" I said to Molly.

36
00:02:33.259 --> 00:02:38.120
"Then just ask her if she and Caswell can watch something different."

37
00:02:38.121 --> 00:02:40.862
"Just ask?" echoed Molly.

38
00:02:40.863 --> 00:02:42.804
She shook her head.

39
00:02:42.805 --> 00:02:46.437
"But that would be admitting I'm a big baby."

40
00:02:46.438 --> 00:02:53.066
"No," I said, "it would be telling Lucy that you don't like monster shows."

41
00:02:53.067 --> 00:02:55.239
Molly looked thoughtful.

42
00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:59.952
"Just ask?" she repeated one more time.

43
00:02:59.953 --> 00:03:04.945
I nodded. "Yep. Just ask."

44
00:03:04.946 --> 00:03:08.810
And that is exactly what Molly did.

45
00:03:08.811 --> 00:03:14.287
She didn't feel like a baby either because Lucy just shrugged and said, "Sure."

46
00:03:14.288 --> 00:03:22.121
And Caswell said, "I'm sick of Monster Madness anyway."

47
00:03:22.122 --> 00:03:28.010
After that Molly started sleeping better.

48
00:03:28.011 --> 00:03:33.520
And Lucy started thinking up stuff for all of us to do after school.

49
00:03:33.521 --> 00:03:36.691
We played games and read books.

50
00:03:36.692 --> 00:03:41.970
We went to the playground and even made a homemade pizza together!

51
00:03:41.971 --> 00:03:48.408
A few weeks later our own books were printed and placed in the school library.

52
00:03:48.409 --> 00:03:53.917
Molly and I were there one day when a second-grade class came in.

53
00:03:53.918 --> 00:03:57.640
The kids started looking for good books to read.

54
00:03:57.641 --> 00:04:02.978
I saw a little girl pick up Jack and the Giant Vacuum.

55
00:04:02.979 --> 00:04:06.893
It was the book that Molly and I had written!

56
00:04:06.894 --> 00:04:14.334
"This book looks really good!" the little girl said to her friend.

57
00:04:14.335 --> 00:04:18.593
And then she sat down and read the whole story!

58
00:04:18.594 --> 00:04:21.851
"Wow," I thought, watching her.

59
00:04:21.852 --> 00:04:28.737
A lot of my inventions, like the Enchanting Cherries bubble bath, turned into big disasters.

60
00:04:28.738 --> 00:04:39.853
But this time, with Molly's help, I had invented something pretty cool—a real page-turner!
